    "q-185293": {
      "dom_id": "step-q185293",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, $\\frac{{2}^{-2}}{{2}^{2}}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{2}^{-2}}{{2}^{2}}={2}^{-2-2}={2}^{-4}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${2}^{-4},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(2)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{2}^{-4}={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{16}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
